{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00942",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.47,
      "end_seconds": 10.28,
      "duration_seconds": 9.81,
      "text": "Ms Okonkwo, the booking says hepatitis B vaccination status. Tell me what's led to this. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.19,
      "end_seconds": 35.36,
      "duration_seconds": 22.17,
      "text": "Yes. I brought notes. I'm starting a placement as a dental nurse on Monday, and the occupational health form needs my hepatitis B immunity status. I had the three injections as a student, but I don't have the paperwork."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.89,
      "end_seconds": 43.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "So you had three doses, but no certificate. When, roughly? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.28,
      "end_seconds": 53.04,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "In 2014, I think. The first, then a month later, then six months after. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.55,
      "end_seconds": 62.87,
      "duration_seconds": 8.32,
      "text": "That's the right schedule. Have you had any symptoms, anything that's made you think of the liver?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.45,
      "end_seconds": 78.24,
      "duration_seconds": 13.79,
      "text": "Not exactly. I've been tired for about two weeks, but I've also been working nights, so, I can't say it means anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.12,
      "end_seconds": 82.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.96,
      "end_seconds": 91.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.82,
      "text": "A bit of nausea last week, after a takeaway. It settled by itself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.07,
      "end_seconds": 101.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.66,
      "text": "So the nausea has gone. Anything else you want to mention before we go on? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.47,
      "end_seconds": 110.5,
      "duration_seconds": 8.03,
      "text": "Not really, I just want the form sorted, I'm that sort of person. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.33,
      "end_seconds": 120.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.24,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about, particularly latex, as you'll be working with gloves?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.79,
      "end_seconds": 134.8,
      "duration_seconds": 12.01,
      "text": "Latex, as a child. I got a rash on my hands from balloons. I haven't had it since, but I always wear nitrile now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.34,
      "end_seconds": 142.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "That's very useful, thank you. Any other health problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.75,
      "end_seconds": 144.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Eczema, mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.02,
      "end_seconds": 150.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "What do you do at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.69,
      "end_seconds": 158.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "I'm a healthcare assistant, nights. I've been doing it for four years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.25,
      "end_seconds": 161.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.75,
      "end_seconds": 167.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "A glass of wine on Fridays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.51,
      "end_seconds": 195.75,
      "duration_seconds": 12.24,
      "text": "Right. Let me check you. Pulse 68, blood pressure 114 over 70, temperature 36.5, oxygen 99 percent, breathing 14, weight 64 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.49,
      "end_seconds": 198.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Normal? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.13,
      "end_seconds": 212.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "All normal. Look up for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.75,
      "end_seconds": 218.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Like this? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.76,
      "end_seconds": 226.9,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "The whites of your eyes are a normal colour, no yellowing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.38,
      "end_seconds": 230.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Good. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.06,
      "end_seconds": 244.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Now I'll press your tummy. Tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.52,
      "end_seconds": 248.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "It's fine. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.66,
      "end_seconds": 257.04,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "Your abdomen is soft and not tender, and I can't feel an enlarged liver."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.59,
      "end_seconds": 260.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "That's reassuring. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.14,
      "end_seconds": 271.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.55,
      "text": "So, no sign of any liver trouble. The tiredness is most likely the night shifts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.32,
      "end_seconds": 277.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "That's what I thought. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.69,
      "end_seconds": 294.59,
      "duration_seconds": 13.9,
      "text": "Let me repeat the plan back. You had three doses in 2014, there's no certificate, and the form needs proof. The way to get it is a blood test. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.38,
      "end_seconds": 299.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Yes. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.44,
      "end_seconds": 310.22,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a hepatitis B surface antibody blood test, and while we're at it, liver function tests."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.43,
      "end_seconds": 315.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "And if the antibody is low? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.61,
      "end_seconds": 325.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "Then we'll discuss a booster. We'll decide on that when the results are back. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.8,
      "end_seconds": 333.9,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "That makes sense. When will the result be ready? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.92,
      "end_seconds": 340.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Usually within a week. Reception will text you. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.07,
      "end_seconds": 346.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Perfect. Will I need to fast? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.9,
      "end_seconds": 352.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "No, you can eat normally. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.77,
      "end_seconds": 355.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Brilliant. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 356.88,
      "end_seconds": 366.72,
      "duration_seconds": 9.84,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in a week to go through the results and sign your form."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.17,
      "end_seconds": 374.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "That works. Monday's my start date, so it's tight, but fine. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.62,
      "end_seconds": 383.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "I'll put it on the form that the result is pending. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 384.98,
      "end_seconds": 389.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. You've been very clear. ~"
    }
  ]
}
